# Phase 18 POP public helper parity — 2026-10-18T11:27:21Z

- Branch: `phase/19-phase-18-compatibility-closure`; base revision `cac0f3e6`.
  Oracle remains Java client 5.5.1 pinned to source marker
  `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.
- Source audit found remaining public helper behavior on the POP headers:
  `PopMessageRequestHeader.getQueueId()` maps all negative values to `-1`,
  `getOrder()` preserves nullable Boolean while `isOrder()` maps null to false,
  and both POP header classes override `toString()` with a selected field list.
- Added Rust equivalents for those helpers and the exact Java-format string
  output. Expanded the invoked Java fixture with default/populated string output,
  negative queue ID, and null/true order cases. Fixture SHA-256:
  `5876a0b734633ff2488d5487df7104fb35ee350b970e1556b0e8c881346a3150`.
- The first strict Protocol Clippy run rejected `assert_eq!(bool, false)` in
  the new regression. Replaced it with `assert!(!...)`; the focused fixture
  differential and strict Protocol Clippy then passed.
